{"id": "EUVD-2026-26503", "enisaUuid": "1c7f26d3-e1fa-3360-96f0-08ffc2704592", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nfuse: reject oversized dirents in page cache\n\nfuse_add_dirent_to_cache() computes a serialized dirent size from the\nserver-controlled namelen field and copies the dirent into a single\npage-cache page. The existing logic only checks whether the dirent fits\nin the remaining space of the current page and advances to a fresh page\nif not. It never checks whether the dirent itself exceeds PAGE_SIZE.\n\nAs a result, a malicious FUSE server can return a dirent with\nnamelen=4095, producing a serialized record size of 4120 bytes. On 4 KiB\npage systems this causes memcpy() to overflow the cache page by 24 bytes\ninto the following kernel page.\n\nReject dirents that cannot fit in a single page before copying them into\nthe readdir cache.", "datePublished": "2026-05-01T13:53:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-15T01:17:53", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7de93abfaae1b2dc94da8a07a36421bd073f1d8f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/474ce83c96a55f2eeb14dee2be375eeadfdacdf5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/51a8de6c50bf947c8f534cd73da4c8f0a13e7bed"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-31694", "GHSA-8fxx-fj7q-42m6"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3b2cf696-436a-33b2-9f43-ffd3affc12cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1"}, {"id": "4aefc322-1447-377c-80a9-93a1d737157f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "895a544c-b6c4-38fc-8c87-c81e9eb21ac3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "b2dbc1c6-436b-3bbd-aac4-dd10c9f2f1e2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27992ef80770d61a57f6c3a551735b08cefdffa3 <474ce83c96a55f2eeb14dee2be375eeadfdacdf5"}, {"id": "b8a3f105-6de3-3fa5-a21c-46fbf201b863", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27992ef80770d61a57f6c3a551735b08cefdffa3 <51a8de6c50bf947c8f534cd73da4c8f0a13e7bed"}, {"id": "d654aebd-a880-37d5-acaf-b6e5ad1587f1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "27992ef80770d61a57f6c3a551735b08cefdffa3 <7de93abfaae1b2dc94da8a07a36421bd073f1d8f"}, {"id": "e8546ed5-c055-3f1b-943d-973d5e29e88b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.0.2"}, {"id": "f187c2af-2490-3a19-a984-8b2172e5deeb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.25"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "1bd06199-b04e-340a-bfb0-7d8ae167fefc", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}